<threat_model>
## Trust Boundaries

| Boundary | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| Browser → API route + tRPC | Authenticated session; user input enters via FormData and tRPC inputs |
| Component → fetch /api/templates/upload | Browser-side fetch; same-origin |
| Component → tRPC | Type-safe, zod-validated inputs |

## STRIDE Threat Register

| Threat ID | Category | Component | Disposition | Mitigation Plan |
|-----------|----------|-----------|-------------|-----------------|
| T-16-23 | Spoofing | Client-side validation bypass (e.g., DevTools removes `.docx` accept filter) | mitigate | Server-side validation in /api/templates/upload (Plan 03) is the source of truth; client-side checks are UX only |
| T-16-24 | Tampering | Client modifies `kategori` to non-enum value before tRPC mutation | mitigate | sablonCreateSchema in tRPC layer (Plan 04) re-validates with z.enum; DB CHECK is final gate (Plan 01) |
| T-16-25 | Information Disclosure | Toast text reflecting raw server error | mitigate | Server errors are pre-authored Turkish strings (no stack traces); component falls back to "Yükleme başarısız. Lütfen tekrar deneyin." for unknown errors |
| T-16-26 | Denial of Service | User uploads many large files in quick succession | accept | Local single-user app; 10 MB cap + sequential mutations make this self-limiting |
| T-16-27 | Repudiation | User claims they did not delete a template | accept | Out of scope per Phase 16 success criteria; sablon-level audit deferred |
</threat_model>

